# /discover-entities

Generalizes Topwater's `/find-companies`. Takes the approved Stage A output
(the {{pipeline.stageA.unitNoun|| "category"}} brief) and pulls a broad,
cheap candidate list of {{vocabulary.entityPlural}} — before any scoring,
before any paid enrichment.

---

## Before anything — reuse check (Rule O4)

Load `standards/OUTPUT-STANDARDS.md` Rule O4. Unit of reuse: the
{{vocabulary.entity}}. A {{vocabulary.entity}} already found by a prior
pull for this {{pipeline.stageA.unitNoun|| "category"}} is not searched for
again; only {{vocabulary.entityPlural}} neither the cached connector pull
nor a prior web sweep found are new.

## Caching (independent of O4 — this is about paid-call cost, not staleness)

Before any new call to a `discovery` connector
({{connectors.discovery}}), check for a cached result from the last 30
days for this exact {{pipeline.stageA.unitNoun|| "category"}}. If one
exists, use it instead of pulling again. This window is unrelated to
whether the answer is "still good" (O4 has no age limit for that) — it
exists purely to avoid paying for the same pull twice inside a month.

---

## What this skill does

1. Reads the approved Stage A brief's `ideal_{{vocabulary.entity}}_profile`
   as the search brief.
2. Pulls a broad candidate list from each configured `discovery` connector
   ({{connectors.discovery}}), respecting each connector's own minimum-field
   discipline (see that connector's `prompt-fragment.md` in
   `templates/connectors/`) — pull broad and cheap here; deep enrichment is
   a later, gated stage.
3. Where more than one `discovery` connector is configured, deduplicates
   {{vocabulary.entityPlural}} across sources before handing the list
   forward.
4. Does not score, tier, or enrich anything in this step — that is the
   scoring stage's job, run separately so nothing gets paid-enriched before
   it's known to qualify.

---

## Output format

Structured JSON only, written to file — this is machine input for the
scoring stage, not a human-facing deliverable
(`standards/OUTPUT-STANDARDS.md` still requires an O2 PDF companion:
render a short readable summary of the pull — count found, sources used,
any connector errors — and PDF that).

```json
{
  "{{pipeline.stageA.unitNoun|| "category"}}": "",
  "pulled_at": "",
  "sources": ["{{connectors.discovery}}"],
  "{{vocabulary.entityPlural}}": [
    { "name": "", "identifier": "", "source": "" }
  ]
}
```

Save per `standards/OUTPUT-STANDARDS.md` Rule O1, under
`outputs/sourcing/<{{pipeline.stageA.unitNoun|| "category"}}-slug>/`.
